<title>CANADA: Toronto stocks jump one percent after Greenspan.</title>
<headline>Toronto stocks jump one percent after Greenspan.</headline>
<text>
<p>CHANGE				     CHANGE</p>
<p>TSE	 6718.00  +70.61   HI 6713.44	    LO  6668.16</p>
<p>DJI	 8058.39 +151.67   GOLD (LONDON)   US$328.25  +2.05</p>
<p>FTSE	4846.70  +41.00   GOLD (COMEX)    US$326.00  -0.20</p>
<p>NIKKEI   20157.02  -92.30   LME CASH NICKEL US$6715     +5.0</p>
<p>CANDLR     1.3780	     LME CASH ALUM   US$1579.0  +25.0</p>
<p>CAN 30-YR  120.22   +1.56   BRENT CRUDE     US$18.22   +0.13</p>
<p>---------------------MARKET COMMENT--------------------------</p>
<p>* Toronto's key stock index soared one percent in late trading on Tuesday after U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan raised expectations that interest rates would stay flat.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
